## PART 5: SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

### 5.1 Authentication & Authorization

- **JWT with expiry:** Access token 1 hour, refresh token 30 days
- **2FA:** TOTP (Google Authenticator, Authy) or SMS OTP
- **Password:** Minimum 12 chars, uppercase, lowercase, digit, special char; hash with bcrypt (rounds: 12)
- **Session:** Only one active session per user (device lock optional)
- **Rate limiting:** 5 failed login attempts → lock 30 minutes
- **Token revocation:** On logout, invalidate tokens

### 5.2 API Security

- **HTTPS only:** All endpoints
- **CORS:** Configure allowed origins (no wildcard *)
- **CSRF Protection:** Include CSRF token in POST/PUT/DELETE requests
- **Input validation:** Server-side validation for all inputs (email regex, phone format, length, special chars)
- **SQL injection:** Use parameterized queries (Django ORM handles this)
- **XSS protection:** Sanitize outputs, use Content Security Policy headers
- **Rate limiting:** 100 requests/minute per IP, per user

### 5.3 Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

- **Super Admin:** Full access (all endpoints)
- **Admin:** Limited (vendors, customers, some analytics; no Super Admin endpoints)
- **Vendor:** Own data only (own bookings, customers, financial; no other vendor data)
- **Customer:** Own data only
- **Enforce at API level:** Middleware checks role and permissions before processing

### 5.4 Data Encryption

- **At rest:** Database encryption (PostgreSQL pgcrypto), sensitive fields encrypted (PAN, bank account, 2FA secret)
- **In transit:** TLS 1.2+ for all API calls
- **Mobile storage:** Keychain (iOS), Keystore (Android) for tokens and PII

### 5.5 Audit & Logging

- **Log all:** Create, Update, Delete, Login, Permission changes
- **Retention:** 1 year
- **Not logged:** Passwords, tokens, PII (only hashed/masked)
- **Access logs:** IP, user agent, timestamp

### 5.6 Compliance

